---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Our method | AIPressHQ"
  description="How AIPressHQ reports, labels, sources, and corrects its AI news coverage."
>
  <section class="standards-page" aria-labelledby="standards-title">
    <header class="standards-header">
      <span class="label">AIPressHQ / editorial standards</span>
      <h1 id="standards-title">Useful context, clearly sourced.</h1>
      <p>
        AIPressHQ is built for readers who want the important development and the evidence needed to
        understand it. We separate what a provider says from what the available evidence supports.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="standards-grid">
      <article class="standards-card">
        <span class="label">01 / Reporting</span>
        <h2>Start with what can be checked.</h2>
        <p>
          We use official documents, product interfaces, research papers, company statements, and
          attributable reporting as the starting point. Each story links to the source that anchors
          its central claim.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="standards-card">
        <span class="label">02 / Formats</span>
        <h2>Label the kind of work you are reading.</h2>
        <p>
          News briefs orient quickly. Explainers build context. Comparisons show tradeoffs. Trackers
          are reviewed as product details change. Analysis makes interpretation visible, and
          tutorials focus on practical steps.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="standards-card">
        <span class="label">03 / Uncertainty</span>
        <h2>Do not fill gaps with confidence.</h2>
        <p>
          Stories call out what is confirmed and what remains open. Availability, limits, pricing,
          and model behavior can vary by account, region, plan, or date, so we tell readers where to
          verify the current state.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="standards-card">
        <span class="label">04 / Corrections</span>
        <h2>Keep the record legible.</h2>
        <p>
          If a factual error is found, we correct the relevant passage and explain the change rather
          than silently replacing the record.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>

    <section class="standards-note" aria-labelledby="standards-note-title">
      <span class="label">A reader's check</span>
      <h2 id="standards-note-title">Read the claim, then follow the source.</h2>
      <p>
        Our goal is not to make every decision for you. It is to make the next verification step
        clear enough that you can make a better one yourself.
      </p>
    </section>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
